<title>USA: Summit Care Q3 March 31 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Summit Care Q3 March 31 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>BURBANK, Calif. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>SUMMIT CARE CORP</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended  Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>					March 31	     March 31</p>
<p>				    1997	 1996  1997(a)     1996</p>
<p> Revenues		    $52,012    $45,232 $147,100 $129,303</p>
<p>Income before income</p>
<p>  taxes			  2,394	2,077    3,247    9,401</p>
<p> Net income		    1,448	1,327    1,964    5,729</p>
<p> Earnings per share	   0.21	 0.19     0.29     0.83</p>
<p> Avg shrs outstanding	6,828	6,849    6,829    6,886</p>
<p>		  (In Thousands, Except Per Share Data)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1997 nine months includes a special charge to revenues and income before income taxes of $4,000,000 and to net income of $2,420,000 or $0.35 per share as a result of adjustments proposed by Medicare in connection with an audit of fiscal 1995 which would also impact fiscal 1996 and the first six months of fiscal 1997.</p>
<p>Net income before the special charge for the first nine months of fiscal 1997 was $4,384,000, or $0.64 per share, compared with $5,729,000, or $0.83 per share, for the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>Newly built and expanded centers had a $0.03 per share negative impact on 1997 Q3 net income, company said.</p>
</text>
